card.statement:
For $\mathbf m=(m_1,\dots, m_n)\in\mathbb Z^n$, and $\mathbf k=(k_1,\dots, k_l)\in \mathbb Z^l$, if $n>l$, then

\begin{equation}
(x_{\mathbf m},x_{\mathbf k}) =0 .
\end{equation}

On the other hand if $n=l$ with

\begin{gather*}
m_1\geq m_2\geq \cdots \geq m_n,\quad k_1\geq k_2\geq \cdots \geq k_n, \\
\sum_{i=1}^nm_i=  \sum_{i=1}^nk_i
\end{gather*}

we have

\begin{equation}
(x_{\mathbf m},x_{\mathbf k}) \equiv\delta_{\mathbf m,\mathbf k}\mod q^2\mathbb Z[\![q]\!].
\end{equation}

and the form is symmetric.
